/-!
# Native local scalar descent on the original period-family total space

A jointly smooth family over a smaller base open defines a genuine
native smooth section on the original full total-space inverse image.
The original period map, quotient projection, and total-space atlas are
unchanged. Smoothness is proved only on this open using the actual
covering local inverses; no boundary-extension regularity is postulated.
-/
